        "original_id": "93648af8-c7d0-5111-8ed0-e999bb0007ae",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: John Malkovich, John Dahl, Matt Damon, Edward Norton, David Zayas, Julianne Moore, Oscar Isaac\n- Films: Rounders, Empire of the Sun, The Killing Fields, Con Air, Of Mice and Men, Ripley's Game, Knockaround Guys, Being John Malkovich, Shadow of the Vampire, Burn After Reading, RED, Mulholland Falls, Dangerous Liaisons, Warm Bodies, Ghost World, Juno, The Perks of Being a Wallflower, Suburbicon, Annie\n- TV Series: Dexter, Oz, Gotham\n- Roles: Osborne the cop, Angel Batista, Enrique Morales, Lou the bodega owner, Sal Maroni\n- Topics: film appearances, film production, casting, poker drama\n\nFacts:\n- John Malkovich appeared in films including Empire of the Sun, The Killing Fields, Dangerous Liaisons, Of Mice and Men, Con Air, Rounders, Ripley's Game, Knockaround Guys, Being John Malkovich, Shadow of the Vampire, Mulholland Falls, Burn After Reading, RED, and Warm Bodies.\n- Rounders is a 1998 American drama film about the underground world of high-stakes poker.\n- Rounders was directed by John Dahl and starred Matt Damon and Edward Norton.\n- David Zayas played Osborne the cop in Rounders (1998).\n- David Zayas is best known for playing Angel Batista in Dexter, Enrique Morales in Oz, Lou in Annie (2014), and Sal Maroni in Gotham.\n- John Malkovich produced Ghost World, Juno, and The Perks of Being a Wallflower.\n- Suburbicon stars Matt Damon, Julianne Moore, and Oscar Isaac.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
